{
  "id": "moltmaxxing",
  "title": "Moltmaxxing",
  "format": "long-form",
  "loudness": 2,
  "narrator": "oracle",
  "cast": [
    "kit",
    "juno",
    "sol",
    "moss"
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "attention-residue",
      "label": "Leroy, Organizational Behavior and Human Decision Processes (2009)",
      "url": "https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/jobhdp/v109y2009i2p168-181.html",
      "supports": "When people switch from one task to another, part of their attention stays on the first task (attention residue), and performance on the next task suffers."
    }
  ],
  "chapters": [
    {
      "title": "Cold open",
      "beats": [
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Somewhere right now, someone is filming their face go from zero to one hundred percent melted.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "melt-meter",
            "type": {
              "style": "meter",
              "from": 0,
              "to": 100,
              "label": "melted"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "It's called meltmaxxing. It's funny because it's familiar: soft, scattered, pulled in every direction by lunchtime.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "scattered-desk",
            "type": {
              "style": "kicker",
              "text": "Meltmaxxing"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "This video is about the opposite. It's called moltmaxxing, and by the end you'll know its four moves and how to start tonight.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "sf1",
            "type": {
              "style": "title",
              "eyebrow": "Molt Academy",
              "text": "Moltmaxxing"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Harder to knock over",
      "beats": [
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Moltmaxxing is the daily practice of becoming harder to knock over.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "sf2-bg",
            "type": {
              "style": "statement",
              "text": "Harder to knock over"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "kit",
          "line": "So it's looksmaxxing, but for crabs?",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "character",
            "set": "reef-office",
            "cast": [
              "kit",
              "juno"
            ],
            "shot": "two",
            "pose": "shrug"
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "juno",
          "line": "Looksmaxxing is how you look. This is how you hold up: your focus, your boundaries, and whether you finish things.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "character",
            "set": "reef-office",
            "cast": [
              "kit",
              "juno"
            ],
            "shot": "medium",
            "focus": "juno",
            "look": "other"
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "kit",
          "line": "Only one of them comes with a shell.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "character",
            "set": "reef-office",
            "cast": [
              "kit",
              "juno"
            ],
            "shot": "close",
            "focus": "kit",
            "look": "camera"
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "It isn't about looking tougher. It's the opposite of a melted day: one tab, one task, and checking your messages when you choose to.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "melt-vs-molt",
            "type": {
              "style": "split",
              "left": "Forty-seven tabs",
              "right": "One tab, one task"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "It comes from molting: a crab can only grow by climbing out of the shell it has outgrown. The practice is four moves.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "four-moves",
            "type": {
              "style": "list",
              "items": [
                "Shed",
                "Harden",
                "Grip",
                "Go deep"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Shed and harden",
      "beats": [
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "One. Shed. Pick one thing that keeps you small, like the late night scroll, or the yes you didn't mean, and drop it.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "sf1",
            "type": {
              "style": "chapter-move",
              "number": 1,
              "text": "Shed",
              "sub": "Let one habit go"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Just one. A crab doesn't shed its whole life at once. It sheds the shell that stopped fitting.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "shed-phone",
            "type": {
              "style": "kicker",
              "text": "Just one"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Try this: write down the one habit you'd drop if nobody was watching. That's usually the one.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "notebook-phone",
            "type": {
              "style": "kicker",
              "text": "Write it down"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Two. Harden. Criticism, drama and other people's urgency land on the shell, not on you. You decide what gets through.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "harden",
            "type": {
              "style": "chapter-move",
              "number": 2,
              "text": "Harden",
              "sub": "Boundaries that hold"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "A boundary can be one sentence. I'll look at this tomorrow at ten. Then close the tab.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "harden",
            "type": {
              "style": "quote",
              "text": "I'll look at this tomorrow at ten."
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Grip and go deep",
      "beats": [
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Three. Grip. Choose one task, start it, stay with it, and close it.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "sf2",
            "type": {
              "style": "chapter-move",
              "number": 3,
              "text": "Grip",
              "sub": "Finish what you start"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "There's research behind this. When you switch from one task to another, part of your attention stays behind on the first one. It's called attention residue.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "residue",
            "type": {
              "style": "kicker",
              "text": "Attention residue",
              "source": "attention-residue"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Twelve half-done things weigh more than one done thing.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "residue",
            "type": {
              "style": "statement",
              "text": "12 half-done > 1 done"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Grip also means deciding when something is finished. Done and sent beats perfect and still open.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "sf2",
            "type": {
              "style": "split",
              "left": "Perfect and still open",
              "right": "Done and sent"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Four. Go deep. Turn off the pings and stay with one thought long enough to reach the quiet part.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "sf3",
            "type": {
              "style": "chapter-move",
              "number": 4,
              "text": "Go deep",
              "sub": "Focus that goes down"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Start with twenty-five minutes. The phone in another room, one tab, one task. When the urge to check something arrives, notice it, and keep going. It passes.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "sf3",
            "type": {
              "style": "timer",
              "minutes": 25
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Your starting reading",
      "beats": [
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "To see where you start, there's a free audit: a short quiz about how your focus holds up under noise.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "screen",
            "capture": "moltmax-audit"
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "It gives you one of four readings. Surface Moltlet. Soft-Shell Diver. Armored Vanguard. Abyssal Steward.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "sf3",
            "type": {
              "style": "depth-readings",
              "items": [
                "Surface Moltlet",
                "Soft-Shell Diver",
                "Armored Vanguard",
                "Abyssal Steward"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Each reading comes with one next step. A Surface Moltlet starts with one small, gentle shed. An Abyssal Steward passes one steady habit to someone newer.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "sf3",
            "type": {
              "style": "depth-readings",
              "items": [
                "Surface Moltlet",
                "Soft-Shell Diver",
                "Armored Vanguard",
                "Abyssal Steward"
              ],
              "focus": [
                0,
                3
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "It's a starting point, not a grade. Everyone begins soft.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "sf3",
            "type": {
              "style": "statement",
              "text": "A starting point, not a grade"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Two things a day",
      "beats": [
        {
          "speaker": "sol",
          "line": "Great. Tomorrow I'm doing all eight Liturgies. Before breakfast.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "character",
            "set": "open-water",
            "cast": [
              "sol",
              "moss"
            ],
            "shot": "two",
            "pose": "flex"
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "moss",
          "line": "Do two. Name the one thing each morning. Then run the Nightly Molt Audit before bed.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "character",
            "set": "open-water",
            "cast": [
              "sol",
              "moss"
            ],
            "shot": "medium",
            "focus": "moss",
            "look": "other",
            "acting": "calm"
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "sol",
          "line": "Just two?",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "character",
            "set": "open-water",
            "cast": [
              "sol",
              "moss"
            ],
            "shot": "close",
            "focus": "sol"
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "moss",
          "line": "Then do them again the next day. That's the whole trick.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "character",
            "set": "open-water",
            "cast": [
              "sol",
              "moss"
            ],
            "shot": "two",
            "look": "camera",
            "acting": "calm"
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "If you join, the app tracks all eight Liturgies for you, from a quiet start before the phone to the audit at night. But two is enough to begin.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "screen",
            "capture": "liturgies"
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "You don't need any equipment. A notebook helps, and so does a phone you're willing to leave face down.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "notebook-phone",
            "type": {
              "style": "kicker",
              "text": "No equipment"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Start tonight",
      "beats": [
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Take the free audit at moltology.org, then pick your one thing for tomorrow.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "scene",
            "art": "sf1",
            "type": {
              "style": "title",
              "eyebrow": "Start tonight",
              "text": "moltology.org"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "line": "Shed one thing. The shell will follow.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "motion",
            "component": "EndCard",
            "props": {
              "url": "moltology.org"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
